"""Standalone report from the tolerance calculation; no SolidWorks needed."""
import html,json,pathlib,sys
p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);x=json.loads(p.read_text());c=x['compression'];w=c['worst_case'];m=c['monte_carlo']
bars=[]
for i,v in enumerate(c['contributors']):
 y=30+i*45
 bars.append(f'<text x="0" y="{y+15}">{html.escape(v["name"])}</text><rect x="180" y="{y}" width="{v["fraction"]*400:.1f}" height="25" fill="#35719c"/><text x="{190+v["fraction"]*400:.1f}" y="{y+18}">{v["fraction"]:.1%}</text>')
body=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Gasket stack-up</title><style>body{{font:17px system-ui;max-width:950px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px}}svg{{width:100%}}pre{{white-space:pre-wrap}}</style><h1>Revision B gasket stack-up</h1><p>Nominal compression {w['nominal']:.1%}. Worst case {w['min']:.1%} to {w['max']:.1%}. The target is 15% to 35%: <strong>{'PASS' if c['passes'] else 'FLAG'}</strong>.</p><p>50,000 bounded independent uniform component samples give mean {m['mean']:.2%} and 1st to 99th percentiles {m['p01']:.2%} to {m['p99']:.2%}. These distributions are assumptions, not measured process capability. Gap is shoulder height minus housing rim height. Its two height tolerances are sampled separately.</p><h2>First-order variance contributors</h2><svg viewBox="0 0 800 230" role="img" aria-label="Tolerance variance contributors">{''.join(bars)}</svg><p>The main contributor is the housing height limit. Tightening it or changing the gland design would need a new calculation and physical verification. The native model uses the nominal dimensions; this report does not establish a seal rating.</p><h2>Thermal screen</h2><p>With {x['thermal']['power_W']} W and assumed natural-convection coefficient {x['thermal']['h_W_m2K']} W/m²K, the single-node rise estimate is {x['thermal']['rise_K']:.1f} K. This ignores internal hotspots and is not a measured temperature.</p><h2>Calculation data</h2><pre>{html.escape(json.dumps(x,indent=2))}</pre></html>'''
p.with_suffix('.html').write_text(body)
